    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i run a small online stationery shop based in lyon and i'm trying to get my paperwork in order for an upcoming audit. can u give me a quick summary of what the main gdpr principles are for a small retailer? mainly interested in how i should be handling customer email addresses and shipping info. thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! GDPR (General Data Protection Regulation) principles primarily focus on five key areas: lawfulness, fairness and transparency, purpose limitation, data minimization, and accuracy, among others. As a small retailer, it's crucial to handle customer contact info such as email addresses and shipping details responsibly. Ensure you obtain explicit storage and processing consent from your customers. Use data solely for the purposes you mentioned (business transactions) and delete or anonymize it when no longer needed. Always keep your systems secure and provide clear information to customers about how their data will be used. These steps should help you meet the GDPR requirements for your stationery shop.",
